{#-
  THE GAME BAR (2026-10-03). One top bar for every game, built here and nowhere else.

  David, 2026-10-03: "a consistent menuing system... for anything from the vital stats games to the
  nurse clicking games, and it's really just like the starting off menus or the top bar." Measured
  the same night: three games drew their own bar (50 or 58px tall, the name at 14, 16 or 17px on a
  phone) and three showed the whole site menu instead. This is Vital Stats' bar, the one he named as
  the best, made into the only one. Plan: docs/HU-CONSISTENCY-TOOLKIT-2026-10-03.md, 2.6.

  The order is fixed: the HU mark, the game's name, an optional tagline (desktop only), then on the
  right the game's own status and action (the caller block: a room chip, a clock, Silence, Walls),
  then the kit's "?" and Menu, mounted by the game's script into the span named by kitId. The site
  menu lives inside Menu (the merged band, so the page sets nav_merged: true); the summon button
  below is kept for the menu's Site menu row to press and is never shown.

  Usage, outside the page's raw block:
    {% from "components/game-bar.njk" import gameBar %}
    {% call gameBar({ name: 'Vital', accent: 'Stats', tagline: 'The healthcare numbers game', kitId: 'vsKit' }) %}
      <span class="vs-roomchip" id="vsRoom" hidden></span>
    {% endcall %}

  Held by tests/game-shell.test.js. Skill: .claude/skills/hu-game-shell.
-#}
{% macro gameBar(g) %}
<header class="tool-bar game-bar">
  <a class="tb-brand" href="/" aria-label="Healthcare Uncharted, home">
    <img src="/brand/hu-mark-dark.svg" alt="" class="hu-logo-ondark">
    <img src="/brand/hu-mark.svg" alt="" class="hu-logo-onlight">
  </a>
  <h1 class="tool-bar-title">{{ g.name }}{% if g.accent %} <span>{{ g.accent }}</span>{% endif %}</h1>
  {% if g.tagline %}<span class="tool-bar-crumb">{{ g.tagline }}</span>{% endif %}
  <span class="tool-bar-spacer"></span>
  <div class="tool-bar-actions">
    {% if caller %}{{ caller() }}{% endif %}
    <span class="game-kit" id="{{ g.kitId }}"></span>
    <button class="icon-btn" data-nav-summon type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Site menu" title="Site menu" tabindex="-1"><i data-lucide="menu" aria-hidden="true"></i></button>
  </div>
</header>
{% endmacro %}
